{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Supercomputer"}, {"type": "position", "content": 12}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to describe important aspects about supercomputers."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts. Make the information system design report, based on the selection of both hardware and software tools required for the IT solution."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understand important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.  Exchange simple information on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob12re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Quantifiers, Enough, Not Enough and Less"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You use <b>quantifiers</b> to describe the amount of something. Some common quantifiers are: <b>enough</b>, <b><i>not enough</i></b><i>,</i> and <b><i>less</i></b>.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p><b>ENOUGH</b></p> <p>You use <b><i>enough</i></b> to indicate that the corresponding amount is satisfactory.</p> <p>Example:&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li><i>Cray had <b>enough </b>experience when he conceived the Data CDC 6600 supercomputer. </i></li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;<b>NOT ENOUGH</b></p> <p>You use <i>not enough </i>to indicate that the corresponding amount is not satisfactory because you need more.</p> <p>&nbsp;Example:</p> <ul> <li>&nbsp;<i>Advances in technology are <b>not enough</b> for computing scientists, so they continue seeking new challenges.</i></li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;<b>LESS</b></p> <p>You use <b><i>less </i></b>to indicate that the corresponding amount is smaller than the expected. Use <b><i>less</i></b> to make inferiority comparisons.</p> <p>&nbsp;Example:</p> <ul> <li>&nbsp;<i>Windows Vista operating system was <b>less</b> popular than Windows XP.</i></li> </ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Seymour Cray had enough experience when he conceived the Data CDC 6600, which had silicon transistors and run at 10 MHz."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was popular but not enough as the Cray I, which was also conceived by Cray in 1976."}, {"type": "example", "content": "However, regarding parallelism, this was less functional than the next supercomputer, the Cray X-MP."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Supercomputers change almost every day, it is not enough for engineers, so they create new machines."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Timeline, The Supercomputer"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Technology has the responsibility to help solving complex tasks in different knowledge domains. For this purpose, engineers work very hard designing supercomputers, mighty machines with special features to perform these tasks.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this timeline, you can check the first supercomputers appearance as well as their gradual progress and improvements up to these days:</p>"}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob12img01.jpg"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "silicon "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "element found in rocks and minerals commonly used in the computer chips manufacture."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: but later in 1964, he had enough experience when he conceived the Data CDC 6600, which had silicon transistors and ran at 10 MHz."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob12aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "vector"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an internal organization of data to be found easily."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This one had a more modern architecture, integrated circuits, and a vector processing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob12aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "parallelism "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "related to computing operations performed by a computer at the same time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This new version was better in terms of parallelism thanks to the incorporation of multiple processors. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob12aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "impose"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to require."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Engineers are constantly creating new inventions in order to improve the existing version and offer solutions to any challenge that science and new generations impose."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob12aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "aircraft"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an air transportation mean, such as an airplane."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They have to develop new machines that can help with aircraft prototypes, the analysis of nuclear effects, the weather models, and other important projects."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob12aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "te